<h2>Segment 277 &mdash; the actual scope of Dharmakirti’s refutation</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s277S"><span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s277q1">der thal</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w1">chos kyi grags pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w2">lung</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w3">don</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p1">ni</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w4">grangs can</span> <span class="u case" data-d="6" data-l="s277p2">gyis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w5">rgyang ring</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w6">thung</span> gi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w7">gzugs</span> la <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w8">bltas pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s277q2">de&#x27;i tshe na</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s277q3">rgyang ring thung</span> gi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w9">gzugs</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p3">dang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w10">mig shes</span> gnyis kyi <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s277q4">bar du</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w11">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w12">gzugs</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w13">gsal</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p4">mi</span> <span class="u unrendered" data-d="5" data-l="s277w14">gsal</span> skye ba&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s277q5">dbang gis</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w15">gzugs</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w16">gsal bar</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w17">snang</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p5">mi</span> <span class="u unrendered" data-d="5" data-l="s277w18">snang</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w19">&#x27;jog pa</span> yin gyi, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w20">gzugs</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s277q6">rnam pa shar ba</span>&#x27;i sgo nas <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w21">gzugs</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w22">gsal bar</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w23">snang</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p6">mi</span> <span class="u unrendered" data-d="5" data-l="s277w24">snang</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w25">&#x27;jog pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w26">ma yin</span> zhes <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w27">khas blangs pa</span> la, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w28">de lta bu</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w29">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w30">gzugs</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w31">gnyis po</span> des <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w32">rgyang ring</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w33">thung</span> gi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w34">gzugs</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w35">gnyis po</span> de <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w36">bsgribs</span> sam <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p7">ma</span> <span class="u unrendered" data-d="5" data-l="s277w37">bsgribs</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w38">bsgribs</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p8">na</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w39">mig shes</span> <span class="u case" data-d="6" data-l="s277p9">kyis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w40">gzugs</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w41">gnyis po</span> de <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p10">ma</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w42">mthong bar</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p11">thal</span>, des de <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w43">sgrib pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p12">phyir</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s277S"><span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s277q1">This is a fact</span>, for the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w3">actual meaning</span> of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w1">Master Dharmakirti</span>&#x27;s <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w2">statement</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p1">is as follows</span>. The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w4">Numerist School</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w27">is describing</span> a <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s277q2">situation where</span> you are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w8">looking</span> at a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w7">physical form</span> either from <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w5">far away</span>, or from <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w6">up close</span>. They say that, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s277q5">depending on</span> the <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s277q3">distance</span> between you and the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w9">object</span>, another <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w12">physical form</span> which is the result of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w11">karma</span>, and which stands <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s277q4">between</span> your <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w10">visual consciousness</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p3">and</span> the original form, is either <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w13">clear</span> or <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p4">not</span>. This then <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w19">determines</span> whether the original <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w15">form</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w17">appears</span> to you <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w16">distinctly</span> or <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p5">not</span>. It <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w26">is not the case</span> though, they say, that what <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w25">determines</span> whether the original <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w21">form</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w23">appears</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w22">clearly</span> or <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p6">not</span> is whether or not you have a clear <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s277q6">impression</span> of this <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w20">form</span>. In reply then Master Dharmakirti is asking the Numerists: Let&#x27;s consider these <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w31">two</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w28">cases</span> of some intermediate <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w30">physical form</span> that comes from <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w29">karma</span>. Do they, or do they <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p7">not</span>, function to <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w36">obscure</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w35">two</span> original <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w34">forms</span>, the one <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w32">at a distance</span>, and the other <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w33">close by</span>? <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p8">If</span> they were to <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w38">obscure</span> them, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p11">then</span> your <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w39">visual consciousness</span> could <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p10">never</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w42">see</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w41">two</span> original <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w40">forms</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p12">since</span> they would have been <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w43">obscured</span> by the others.<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p2"><span class="nul">Agentive asserter is represented by English active subject; there is no independent by.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w14"><span class="nul">Second clarity predicate is shared by English clear or not [clear]; no second printed clear in this alternative.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w18"><span class="nul">Repeated negative-side appearance predicate has no separate exponent in appears ... or not.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w24"><span class="nul">Second negative-side appearance verb is elliptical in English appears clearly or not; not absent in meaning.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s277w37"><span class="nul">English shares the single function to obscure predicate across positive/negative question branches; no second printed obscure in that question.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s277p9"><span class="nul">Active seeing subject incorporates agentive role; no independent by in this clause.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first original informed by its own earlier source preparation; the independent current English original has not been read. Original forms, intermediate forms and observers keep their separate occurrences despite English reversals. The second distance phrase is retained at phrase depth, while the final far qualifier is provisionally proposed as at a distance and requires skeptical review. The complete arising-aspect expression is retained as impression; clear stays unwrapped despite the positive rnam pa glossary variant. The appearance clarity adverbs belong to their own clauses. Repeated gsal, snang and the negative-question bsgribs have no separately printed exponent because English shares their positive predicate across or not; these are ellipsis nulls, not uncertainty labels. The sole Tibetan name and Numerist assertion own one English occurrence each. Intermediate, original, object participants, whether-or-not scaffolding, skye ba existence/result expansion, yin gyi contrast and redundant pronouns are omitted where distributed or supplied. Source wording and hgm_gloss remain unchanged; reconciliation and semantic review are still required.</div>
